- h1-late-queued-pipeline-never-promoted (libwebsockets/lib/sansio/vhost.c:927-960, lws_client_connect_4 queueing;
  libwebsockets/lib/sansio/wsi.c:2030-2135, _lws_generic_transaction_completed_active_conn): a second
  HTTP/1.1 client request queued with LCCSCF_PIPELINE onto a connection whose first transaction had
  already completed (idle) was never sent in the old lws (ollama-repl "only the first prompt works").
  The vendored lws no longer has the old layout: vhost.c now hands an idle LRS_IDLING h1 leader's
  connection to the queued request right away, and I could not reproduce the symptom here.

    2026-11-25: checked with lib/fetch.js (keepAlive, LCCSCF_PIPELINE) against a python HTTP/1.1
    keep-alive server, 3 POSTs per run, gaps of 0, 2, 4.5, 5.5, 8 and 30 s: all succeed, the
    connection is reused up to the 5 s keep_warm_secs default (io/client/connect.c:219) and a fresh
    one is opened after it, so a 90 s idle connection is never reused anyway. Not tested: the real Ollama server and a
    black-holed connection (no FIN or RST ever arrives). Left open until someone confirms it
    against the real Ollama server (qjsm examples/ollama-repl/repl.js --provider ollama, with the
    PIPELINE-less workaround in examples/ollama-repl/lib/*-client.js reverted); remove the entry if
    that works. lib/fetch.js:139 still enables LCCSCF_PIPELINE by default, so ordinary fetch()
    users would be exposed if the bug were real.

- vhost-destroy-logs-spurious-not-on-no-listener-list-error
  (libwebsockets/lib/core-net/vhost.c:1706-1707, __lws_vhost_destroy2()):
  destroying any vhost logs "ERR [vh|N|name||-1]: not on no_listener list"
  unconditionally unless the vhost is on `no_listener_vlist` - but a vhost
  only ever gets added to that list from server.c's `sockfd_probe_listener()`
  path, gated on `a->vhost->iface` being set (binding to one specific
  network interface). A normal vhost (no `iface` option - the common case,
  including every vhost this project creates) never takes that path, so
  it's permanently "not on the list" and this fires every single time such
  a vhost is destroyed. Cosmetic/harmless - not an actual error, nothing is
  broken - just noisy: confirmed by reading vhost.c/server.c, not something
  worth patching in the vendored libwebsockets submodule without being
  asked. Running tests/test-jsonrpc-ws.js prints it 3 times: once each for
  the "default" and implicit "system" vhosts of the main server context at
  shutdown, and once for a second client context's default vhost - named
  after the machine's hostname since no `vhostName` was passed - torn down
  later and asynchronously by ContextRefCounter (lib/lws/context.js) once
  its ref count hits zero after the reversed-roles self-test's
  `reverseWs.close()`, which is why that third one appears interleaved with
  later output (e.g. after the REPL banner) instead of at the same point in
  the script.

    // any LWSContext without an `iface` option on its vhost(s) logs this
    // on destroy; e.g. just running tests/test-jsonrpc-ws.js reproduces it.

- serve-websocket-options-silently-ignored (lib/serve.js:~640): backpressureLimit, closeOnBackpressureLimit and sendPings are read and never used (perMessageDeflate, maxPayloadLength and publishToSelf work now); they need the write queue size / ping control from lws.

- check-cflag-result-cached-under-fixed-name (cmake/Checks.cmake:19, check_cflag()): result stored
  in the shared cache variable RESULT, so every probe after the first one returns the first answer.
  Full description and repro in qjs-modules/BUGS (identical copy of the function).

- lws-termux-flag-not-applied (cmake/BuildLibwebsockets.cmake:381-385): the Termux branch appends
  " -DTERMUX=TRUE" to LIBWEBSOCKETS_ARGS, a string, and that reaches ExternalProject without a
  cache type, so CMake 4.5 prints "Line 'TERMUX=TRUE' does not match regex.  Ignoring." and the
  libwebsockets build never sees TERMUX. patches/0004-termux-resolvconf.patch only adds
  -DTERMUX_PREFIX under `if (TERMUX)`, so the Termux resolv.conf path is not applied. Found
  2026-11-15 on a fresh Termux. Fix: -DTERMUX:BOOL=TRUE (every other -D in that list has a type).

    cmake -S . -B build/x   # on Termux, look for "Line 'TERMUX=TRUE' does not match regex"

- lws-endif-arguments-mismatch (cmake/BuildLibwebsockets.cmake:387-392 and 394-396): `if(WIN32 AND
  NOT MSYS)` is closed by `endif(WIN32)`; CMake 4.5 warns "A logical block opening on the line ...
  closes on the line ... with mis-matching arguments" on every configure. Harmless, noisy.

- lws-externalproject-cmp0225 (cmake/BuildLibwebsockets.cmake:568): ExternalProject_Add(websockets_shared
  / websockets_static) uses the default configure command without CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX; CMake 4.5
  warns (policy CMP0225) and the NEW behaviour would change the install prefix of the nested build.
  Set the policy or pass CMAKE_INSTALL_PREFIX explicitly.

- compact-single-turn (examples/ollama-repl/repl.js:3760): compactHook with one long user turn (a job with ~11 tool calls) summarizes the whole turn down to 2 messages, so the running job loses its context (reported after a model switch to a smaller context window)

    ollama-repl --compact-at 1 and send one prompt that makes the model call ~10 tools
